\section{Model}
We minimize the contrastive objective
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:loss}
\mathcal{L} = -\log \frac{\exp(s^+/\tau)}{\exp(s^+/\tau) + \exp(s^-/\tau)} .
\end{equation}
Equation~\ref{eq:loss} is computed per anchor.

\section{Experiments}
We ablate the temperature in Eq.~\ref{eq:loss} from 0.05 to 0.5.
The gradient of Eq.~\ref{eq:loss} vanishes when negatives are too easy.

